{
  "name": "bias-disambiguation",
  "description": "Same-name place disambiguation under proximity bias. Each ambiguous toponym (Cambridge, Aurora, Arlington, Springfield, Portland, Salem, Newcastle, Cornwall, Frankfurt, ...) has 2-4 cases — one per major candidate. The bias hint is placed near the EXPECTED candidate; if the bias-aware ranker picks the wrong sibling, the coord_within_m check fails. Surfaces regressions in the boosted_score curve (piecewise distance penalty) and the importance bonus.\n\nTolerance is 10 km — loose enough to absorb place_point centroid vs admin polygon centroid drift, tight enough to catch wrong-candidate selection (ambiguous siblings are typically 100s of km apart).\n\nOriginal source: bench-accuracy failures (Arlington VA, Aurora US, Cornwall CA, Münster DE, Greensboro US, Vic ES, Figtree AU) plus standard same-name targets known from Pelias/Nominatim documentation.",
  "cases": [
    {
      "id": "bias-disamb-cambridge-ma",
      "tags": ["search", "bias", "disambiguation"],
      "request": {
        "path": "/search",
        "query": {
          "q": "Cambridge",
          "country_code": "us",
          "bias_lat": "42.36",
          "bias_lng": "-71.06"
        }
      },
      "expect": {
        "status": 200,
        "checks": [
          { "kind": "json_path_min_count", "path": "results", "min": 1 },
          {
            "kind": "coord_within_m",
            "lat_path": "results.0.lat",
            "lng_path": "results.0.lon",
            "expected_lat": 42.37,
            "expected_lng": -71.11,
            "max_m": 10000
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
